 ithub.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Electricity%20Basics%20%2B%20Safe
 ty%20%2B%20Ohm/Watt\n• Lab Center: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-un
 iversity/labs.html\n• Assessment Center: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alf
 red-university/assessments.html\n• Engineering Library: https://nberclaw
 2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Foundatio
 nal circuit measurement and safe troubleshooting.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa
  Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; us
 e Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LIN
 KS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Go
 ogle Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 
 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nAFTER TODA
 Y — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES\nBy the end of this event\, you should be
  able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Know what equipment/parts are requir
 ed for the next practical session and what each item is for.\n• Confirm 
 every critical item is ready\, compatible\, and safe to use before the lab
  begins.\n• Identify any missing item early enough to obtain or substitu
 te it without cancelling the hands-on work.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigne
 d resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outco
 me list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items aft
 er the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on 
 a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resource
  before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned wo
 rk\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demo
 nstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and r
 epair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is
  required.
