SUMMARY:W01 • Learn — Electricity\, Safety & Ohm’s Law
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfr
 ed-university/week.html?week=1\n• Search this topic: https://numberclaw2.g
 ithub.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Electricity%20Basics%20%2B%20Safe
 ty%20%2B%20Ohm/Watt\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/
 alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Foundational circuit 
 measurement and safe troubleshooting.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Ca
 reer Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive 
 for repair or extra depth.\n\nSTART FROM ZERO — SESSION 1\nWHY THIS STAR
 TS HERE: Every later embedded-system skill assumes you understand what vol
 tage\, current\, resistance\, power\, ground\, polarity\, open circuits\, 
 shorts\, and safe measurement mean. We are not assuming prior electronics 
 knowledge.\n\nWEEK 1 FOCUS: START FROM ZERO: Safety + What Electricity Is 
 + Voltage / Current / Resistance + Ohm / Watt + SI Prefixes\nETA/CETa SCOP
 E — FIRST PASS: 1.1\, 1.4–1.7\, 1.10\, 1.13–1.14\; 2.1\, 2.4\, 2.6\,
  2.13–2.14\; 9.8–9.9. The narrower RF/fiber/field-safety details retur
 n later in CETa-specific review.\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Build the vocab
 ulary and safety habits every later circuit\, instrument\, microcontroller
 \, and troubleshooting skill depends on. Set up the Git evidence notebook 
 from day one.\n\nTODAY — 8:00 PM TO 9:30 PM:\n1. Safety first (10 min): 
 electrical shock basics\, de-energizing\, ESD\, and why resistance measure
 ments are made on de-energized circuits.\n2. What electricity is (15 min):
  charge/electrons at a practical technician level\; do not get buried in a
 tomic physics.\n3. Learn voltage vs current vs resistance vs power (25 min
 ). Explain each in your own words before moving on.\n4. Open the ETA Commo
 n Formulas sheet and locate Ohm's law / power relationships (5 min).\n5. W
 ork 6–8 beginner Ohm/Watt problems with units (15 min). Show the rearran
 gement\; do not copy an example.\n6. Set up or confirm the GitHub lab note
 book/repository (10 min). Create a Week_01 folder/note.\n\nMASTERY GATE: I
 n plain language\, explain charge\, voltage\, current\, resistance\, power
 \, polarity\, open vs short\, and basic ESD/shock precautions\; use SI pre
 fixes\; solve fresh Ohm/Watt problems\; then build and safely measure a cu
 rrent-limited LED circuit on Saturday.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Learn from the bot
 tom. Watching alone never counts. Use learn → retrieve → calculate/cod
 e → build/measure → debug → document. Start later study blocks with 
 ~10 minutes of spaced recall. A missed session never creates an unhealthy 
 make-up marathon.\n\nWEEK 1 START-FROM-ZERO RESOURCES:\n• Electric Curre
 nt and Circuits Explained: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r-SCyD7f_zI\n
 • Electrical Safety Training: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TMT6f3tZQS
 k\n• GitHub Skills — Introduction to GitHub: https://github.com/skills
 /introduction-to-github\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Offici
 al Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy
  and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata:
  https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — 
 V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.1 pp.1–6 SKIM only\; Ch.2 pp.7–14\;
  Ch.3 pp.16–18\; Ch.4 pp.25–26\; read the book addendum once.\nQUIZ / 
 REVIEW: Ch.2 quiz p.15 after the safety lesson. Use answers p.223 only aft
 er finishing.\nWHY: Starts from zero with safety\, units\, Ohm/Watt and th
 e physical meaning of voltage/current/resistance before circuit analysis.\
 nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current E
 TA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book
  differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OU
 TCOMES (WEEK 01)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain
  or demonstrate:\n• Explain voltage\, current\, resistance\, power\, gro
 und/reference\, polarity\, open circuits\, and short circuits.\n• Use SI
  prefixes and engineering notation correctly for common electronic values.
 \n• Apply Ohm's law and the Watt/power relationships to simple DC circui
 ts.\n• Recognize basic electrical hazards and use safe low-voltage measu
 rement habits.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above a
 re intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot 
 explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not count
  that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use
  the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nS
 IMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning 
 outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write th
 at one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next avai
 lable review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
