 rom zero with safety\, units\, Ohm/Watt and the physical meaning of voltag
 e/current/resistance before circuit analysis.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-editio
 n book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + curr
 ent ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or omits a current 
 topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 01)\nBy the end
  of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Solve 
 Ohm's law and power problems with units and SI prefixes.\n• Predict curr
 ent\, voltage drop\, resistance\, and power before measuring.\n• Explain
  why current limiting and correct meter connections matter.\n\nCOVERAGE AU
