 extbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whene
 ver the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — RE
 QUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 01)\nBy the end of this event\, you should 
 be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Explain voltage\, current\, resist
 ance\, power\, ground/reference\, polarity\, open circuits\, and short cir
 cuits.\n• Use SI prefixes and engineering notation correctly for common 
 electronic values.\n• Apply Ohm's law and the Watt/power relationships t
 o simple DC circuits.\n• Recognize basic electrical hazards and use safe
  low-voltage measurement habits.\n• Solve Ohm's law and power problems w
 ith units and SI prefixes.\n• Predict current\, voltage drop\, resistanc
 e\, and power before measuring.\n• Explain why current limiting and corr
 ect meter connections matter.\n• Relate calculated voltage/current/power
  to what a DMM measures on a real circuit.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned
  resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcom
 e list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items afte
 r the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a
