DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfr
 ed-university/week.html?week=2\n• Search this topic: https://numberclaw2.g
 ithub.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=DC%20Networks%20%2B%20KVL/KCL%20%
 2B%20Voltage%20Dividers%20%2B%20DMM\n• Engineering Library: https://nber
 claw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Found
 ational circuit measurement and safe troubleshooting.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: 
 CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\
 ; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 2 FOCUS: DC Networks + 
 KVL/KCL + Voltage Dividers +DMM\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 4.1\; 4.10\; 4.17\; 3.1.4
 \; 8.1–8.4\; 8.16\;9.1–9.2\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Series/parallel n
 etworks\,voltage/current division\, meter range/connection\, LTspice predi
 ctionvs measurement.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- Electronic Circuitsplayl
 ist: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL0o_zxa4K1BV9E-N8tSExU1djL6sln
 jbL\n- ETA Common Formulas:https://www.etai.org/Common_Formulas.pdf\n- LTs
 pice:https://www.analog.com/en/resources/design-tools-and-calculators/ltsp
 ice-simulator.html\n\nMASTERY GATE: Solve unseen series/parallel/KVL/KCLpr
 oblems\, predict test points\, then verify a built divider networkwith DMM
  and explain any measurement error.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watchingalone never c
 ounts. Use learn -> retrieve -> calculate/code ->build/measure -> debug ->
  document. Start each non-exam study block with~10 minutes of spaced recal
 l. Never use a missed session asjustification for an unhealthy make-up mar
 athon.\n\nTODAY:\nStudy onlythe resources tied to this week’s competenci
 es. Create a one-pagesummary and 5–10 recall prompts. First 10 min: spac
 ed retrieval fromolder material.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n
 • Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google 
 Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-e
 d. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY 
 GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.3 p.19 series/parallel formul
 as + Ch.4 pp.27–34.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.4 quiz p.34\, then Unit 2 review 
 p.35.\nWHY: The book's DC-circuit sequence aligns directly with series/par
 allel\, KVL/KCL\, voltage dividers and troubleshooting.\nSOURCE RULE: The 
 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency word
 ing + current ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or omits 
 a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 02)\n
 By the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n
 • Analyze series and parallel resistor networks.\n• Use Kirchhoff's Vo
 ltage Law and Kirchhoff's Current Law to reason about circuit behavior.\n
 • Design and analyze a voltage divider\, including the effect of loading
 .\n• Predict node voltages\, branch currents\, equivalent resistance\, a
 nd power.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are in
 tended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot expla
 in or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not count that
  item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the 
 linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE
  COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning outco
 mes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that on
 e concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next available
  review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
