 st: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL0o_zxa4K1BV9E-N8tSExU1djL6slnj
 bL\n- ETA Common Formulas:https://www.etai.org/Common_Formulas.pdf\n- LTsp
 ice:https://www.analog.com/en/resources/design-tools-and-calculators/ltspi
 ce-simulator.html\n\nMASTERY GATE: Solve unseen series/parallel/KVL/KCLpro
 blems\, predict test points\, then verify a built divider networkwith DMM 
 and explain any measurement error.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watchingalone never co
 unts. Use learn -> retrieve -> calculate/code ->build/measure -> debug -> 
 document. Start each non-exam study block with~10 minutes of spaced recall
 . Never use a missed session asjustification for an unhealthy make-upmarat
 hon.\n\nTODAY:\nBuild/measure/debug the practical objective.Photograph or 
 capture evidence\, document expected vs actual\, andcommit the lab note/co
 de. Completion requires demonstration\, notwatching.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — 
 KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use y
 our scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNM
 ENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf
 \n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.3 p.19 ser
 ies/parallel formulas + Ch.4 pp.27–34.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.4 quiz p.34\, 
 then Unit 2 review p.35.\nWHY: The book's DC-circuit sequence aligns direc
 tly with series/parallel\, KVL/KCL\, voltage dividers and troubleshooting.
 \nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current 
 ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older boo
 k differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING O
 UTCOMES (WEEK 02)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explai
 n or demonstrate:\n• Analyze series and parallel resistor networks.\n•
  Use Kirchhoff's Voltage Law and Kirchhoff's Current Law to reason about c
 ircuit behavior.\n• Design and analyze a voltage divider\, including the
  effect of loading.\n• Predict node voltages\, branch currents\, equival
 ent resistance\, and power.\n• Calculate equivalent resistance\, node/br
 anch values\, divider outputs\, and power.\n• Use KVL/KCL to check wheth
 er calculated results are internally consistent.\n• Use a DMM to verify 
 a DC network and explain differences between predicted and measured values
 .\n• Troubleshoot opens\, shorts\, wrong resistor values\, and wiring mi
 stakes systematically.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks
  above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still
  cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do n
 ot count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list
  and use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the g
 ap.\n\nWEEK-END MASTERY RULE\nThis practical is the cumulative proof point
  for the week. The week is Green only when the knowledge can be used on re
 al hardware/code/measurements without following a step-by-step tutorial.\n
 \nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learni
 ng outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write
  that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next a
 vailable review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
