 pages\; no answer-key checking until you have committed answers.\nWHY: Bui
 lds AC waveform\, RMS\, frequency/period\, capacitance\, inductance and fi
 rst-order reactive behavior.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the pri
 mary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata co
 ntrol whenever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER T
 ODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 04)\nBy the end of this event\, 
 you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Describe sine waves and
  basic AC quantities: amplitude\, peak\, peak-to-peak\, frequency\, period
 \, phase\, and RMS.\n• Convert between frequency and period and interpre
 t waveform measurements.\n• Explain how capacitors and inductors store e
 nergy and oppose changes in voltage or current.\n• Describe RC and RL tr
 ansient behavior and the idea of a time constant.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe a
