 cribe RC and RL transient behavior and the idea of a time constant.\n• C
 alculate frequency/period\, RMS or peak relationships where assigned\, and
  basic RC timing quantities.\n• Read waveform scales accurately and conn
 ect numerical results to scope displays.\n• Recognize basic low-pass and
  high-pass behavior.\n• Use an oscilloscope to connect waveform theory t
 o measured circuit behavior.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and
  tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you
  still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\
 , do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-u
 p list and use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing
  the gap.\n\nWEEK-END MASTERY RULE\nThis practical is the cumulative proof
  point for the week. The week is Green only when the knowledge can be used
  on real hardware/code/measurements without following a step-by-step tutor
 ial.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the 
 learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\,
  write that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the 
 next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
