 : https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CON
 NECTION: Component-level analog/digital troubleshooting and instrumentatio
 n.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete t
 he required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 
 6 FOCUS: Reactance + Impedance + Resonance + Filters +Transformers\nETA/CE
 Ta SCOPE: 2.1–2.5.1\; 2.10–2.11\; 3.4–3.4.2\;4.7–4.16\; 9.6\nCAREE
 R/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Understand filters\,clocks/crystals\, inductive loads\
 , transformer behavior\, resonance andbandwidth/Q without over-specializin
 g.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n-Capacitors and Inductors playlist:https://w
 ww.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLB9A78ED3D7EF1AE5\n- Oscillatorsand Multivib
 rators playlist:https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLwjK_iyK4LLCVdgBR30
 pSFVj-17TI_8ou\n- ETA Common Formulas:https://www.etai.org/Common_Formulas
 .pdf\n\nMASTERY GATE: Calculatereactance/resonance\, classify an RLC netwo
 rk\, explain transformerstep-up/down and crystal/oscillator purpose\, and 
 interpret a simplefilter response.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never c
 ounts. Use learn-> retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug ->
  document.Start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recal
 l. Neveruse a missed session as justification for an unhealthy make-upmara
 thon.\n\nTODAY:\nStudy only the resources tied to this week’scompetencie
