 for Beginners:https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLzqS33DOPhJkRn6e9_OTd
 QwRojO8qlusI\n- NMOS vs PMOS / Enhancement vs Depletion:https://www.youtub
 e.com/watch?v=kY-ka0PriaE\n- ETA CETa competencies:https://www.etai.org/co
 mps/CETa_comps.pdf\n\nMASTERY GATE: Identifydevices and terminals\, analyz
 e simple bias/current/power\, select atransistor/MOSFET as a switch\, and 
 troubleshoot one intentionallymiswired circuit.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching 
 alone never counts. Uselearn -> retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measur
 e -> debug ->document. Start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of
  spacedrecall. Never use a missed session as justification for an unhealth
 ymake-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nBuild/measure/debug the practicalobjective. 
 Photograph or capture evidence\, document expected vsactual\, and commit t
 he lab note/code. Completion requiresdemonstration\, not watching.\n\nREFE
 RENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 
 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers i
 n BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTE
 rrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE:
  Ch.9 pp.70–78 + Ch.10 pp.79–83.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.9 quiz p.78\, Ch.1
 0 quiz p.83 and Unit 4 review p.84.\nWHY: Directly supports semiconductor 
 recognition\, switching behavior and discrete-device troubleshooting.\nSOU
 RCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA c
 ompetency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book dif
 fers or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOM
 ES (WEEK 08)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or 
 demonstrate:\n• Explain PN junction behavior and the operation/use of re
 ctifier diodes\, LEDs\, Zener diodes\, and protection diodes.\n• Explain
  BJT switching at a practical level and distinguish NPN/PNP behavior.\n•
  Explain FET/MOSFET gate control\, source/drain roles\, logic-level switch
 ing\, and common protection concerns.\n• Recognize SCR/TRIAC purpose and
  where controlled switching devices are used.\n• Reason about diode drop
 s\, current limiting\, transistor/MOSFET switching conditions\, and device
  ratings.\n• Recognize whether a semiconductor device is being used safe
 ly within its stated limits.\n• Select and wire a basic transistor/MOSFE
 T switch with appropriate current limiting/flyback protection.\n• Troubl
 eshoot common semiconductor-switching faults with a meter or scope.\n\nCOV
 ERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover 
 every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrat
 e one of these items after the session\, do not count that item as complet
 e. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked official 
 or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nWEEK-END MASTERY RULE\
 nThis practical is the cumulative proof point for the week. The week is Gr
 een only when the knowledge can be used on real hardware/code/measurements
  without following a step-by-step tutorial.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFin
 ish the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you can
 not explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short 
 catch-up list and repair it during the next available review block. No spr
 eadsheet logging is required.
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
