 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfr
 ed-university/week.html?week=9\n• Search this topic: https://numberclaw2.g
 ithub.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Electronic%20Power%20Supplies\n
 • Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/res
 ources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Component-level analog/digital troubleshoo
 ting and instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core 
 → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair
  or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 9 FOCUS: Power Supplies + Rectifiers + Regulation
  +Protection\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 10.1–10.11\; 1.4\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE:
 Power trees\, linear vs switching supply\,rectification/filtering/regulati
 on\, fuse/protection placement\, 3.3V/5Vrail awareness.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RES
 OURCES:\n- Linear Power Supply:https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UTetQhGyUVg
 \n- Switch-Mode Power Supply:https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3FyXqNcqvRM\n
 - ETA Common Formulas:https://www.etai.org/Common_Formulas.pdf\n\nMASTERY 
 GATE: Trace asupply block diagram\, calculate expected DC outputs\, identi
 fyrectifier/filter/regulator stages\, and isolate one likely supplyfault.\
 n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn ->retrieve -> calc
 ulate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> document. Starteach non-exam study
  block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use amissed session as jus
 tification for an unhealthy make-upmarathon.\n\nTODAY:\nStudy only the res
 ources tied to this week’scompetencies. Create a one-page summary and 5
 –10 recall prompts. First10 min: spaced retrieval from older material.\n
 \nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Gu
 ide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page num
 bers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6th
 EdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD 
 / USE: Ch.11 pp.85–90.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.11 quiz p.90.\nWHY: The entire
  chapter maps cleanly to power-supply architecture\, rectification\, filte
 ring\, regulation and faults.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the pr
 imary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata c
 ontrol whenever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER 
 TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 09)\nBy the end of this event\,
  you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Describe the functiona
 l blocks of an electronic power supply: transformation/conversion\, rectif
 ication\, filtering\, regulation\, and protection.\n• Explain half-wave/
 full-wave/bridge rectification and the purpose of filter capacitors.\n• 
 Distinguish basic linear regulation from switching regulation.\n• Explai
 n ripple\, load regulation\, line regulation\, efficiency\, and current li
 miting at a practical level.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and
  tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you
  still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\
 , do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-u
 p list and use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing
  the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check
  the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outc
 ome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during
  the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
