DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfr
 ed-university/week.html?week=9\n• Search this topic: https://numberclaw2.g
 ithub.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Electronic%20Power%20Supplies\n
 • Lab Center: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/labs.html\n
 • Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/res
 ources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Component-level analog/digital troubleshoo
 ting and instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core 
 → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair
  or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 9 FOCUS: Power Supplies + Rectifiers + Regulation
  +Protection\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 10.1–10.11\; 1.4\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE:
 Power trees\, linear vs switching supply\,rectification/filtering/regulati
 on\, fuse/protection placement\, 3.3V/5Vrail awareness.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RES
 OURCES:\n- Linear Power Supply:https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UTetQhGyUVg
 \n- Switch-Mode Power Supply:https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3FyXqNcqvRM\n
 - ETA Common Formulas:https://www.etai.org/Common_Formulas.pdf\n\nMASTERY 
 GATE: Trace asupply block diagram\, calculate expected DC outputs\, identi
 fyrectifier/filter/regulator stages\, and isolate one likely supplyfault.\
 n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn ->retrieve -> calc
 ulate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> document. Starteach non-exam study
  block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use amissed session as jus
 tification for an unhealthy make-upmarathon.\n\nTODAY:\nBuild/measure/debu
 g the practical objective.Photograph or capture evidence\, document expect
 ed vs actual\, andcommit the lab note/code. Completion requires demonstrat
 ion\, notwatching.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official As
 sociate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and 
 the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: http
 s://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BO
 OK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.11 pp.85–90.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.11 quiz p.
 90.\nWHY: The entire chapter maps cleanly to power-supply architecture\, r
 ectification\, filtering\, regulation and faults.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-ed
 ition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + 
 current ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or omits a curr
 ent topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 09)\nBy the
  end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• De
 scribe the functional blocks of an electronic power supply: transformation
 /conversion\, rectification\, filtering\, regulation\, and protection.\n
 • Explain half-wave/full-wave/bridge rectification and the purpose of fi
 lter capacitors.\n• Distinguish basic linear regulation from switching r
 egulation.\n• Explain ripple\, load regulation\, line regulation\, effic
 iency\, and current limiting at a practical level.\n• Calculate or estim
 ate rectified/filter/regulator output and basic power/efficiency/ripple re
 lationships at assigned depth.\n• Use measured rails to isolate which su
 pply block is failing.\n• Recognize protection devices and likely failur
 e points in a supply.\n• Measure input/output rails and use symptoms to 
 isolate a power-supply fault.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources an
 d tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If yo
 u still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session
 \, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-
 up list and use the linked official or supplemental resource before closin
 g the gap.\n\nWEEK-END MASTERY RULE\nThis practical is the cumulative proo
 f point for the week. The week is Green only when the knowledge can be use
 d on real hardware/code/measurements without following a step-by-step tuto
 rial.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the
  learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\
 , write that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the
  next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
