DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfr
 ed-university/week.html?week=10\n• Search this topic: https://numberclaw2.
 github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Amplifiers%20%2B%20Op-Amps%20%2B
 %20Gain\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-unive
 rsity/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Component-level analog/digital tr
 oubleshooting and instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Caree
 r Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for
  repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 10 FOCUS: Amplifiers + Op-Amps + Gain +Loa
 ding\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 11.1–11.9\; 9.6\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE:Analog si
 gnal conditioning for sensors\; gain\, feedback\,saturation/distortion\, b
 andwidth\, scope/meter loading.\n\nTHIS WEEK'SRESOURCES:\n- Transistor Bia
 s & Amplifier Classes:https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c6cmkm3UPUI\n- Op-Am
 p Circuits:https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K03Rom3Cs28\n- Common-Emitter G
 ain &Frequency Response: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NizrzRKQqII\n\nMA
 STERY GATE: Calculate basic gain\, distinguish amplifier classes and op-am
 proles\, predict clipping/loading\, and measure an analog stage withoutcor
 rupting it.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn-> retr
 ieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> document.Start each no
 n-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Neveruse a missed se
 ssion as justification for an unhealthy make-upmarathon.\n\nTODAY:\nStudy 
 only the resources tied to this week’scompetencies. Create a one-page su
 mmary and 5–10 recall prompts. First10 min: spaced retrieval from older 
 material.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate C
 ET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINT
 ED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.e
 tai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGN
 MENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.12 pp.91–101.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.12 quiz p.101 + Un
 it 5 review pp.102–103.\nWHY: Provides the CETa analog-amplifier and dB 
 foundation\; labs add the practical embedded signal-conditioning angle.\nS
 OURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA
  competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book d
 iffers or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTC
 OMES (WEEK 10)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain o
 r demonstrate:\n• Explain voltage gain\, current gain\, power gain\, loa
 ding\, input/output impedance\, and feedback.\n• Use decibels at a basic
  technician level and relate dB changes to gain/loss.\n• Distinguish com
 mon amplifier classes and basic transistor/FET amplifier roles.\n• Expla
 in ideal op-amp assumptions at an introductory level.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nT
 he assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in 
 this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these
  items after the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the c
 oncept on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplementa
 l resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the a
 ssigned work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot expla
 in or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up 
 list and repair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet 
 logging is required.
