 FICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.16 pp.132–143.
 \nQUIZ / REVIEW: Hold the full Ch.16 quiz until W14 after computer-basics 
 pages are finished.\nWHY: Covers number systems\, logic families\, gates\,
  Boolean logic and sequential circuits before MCU work.\nSOURCE RULE: The 
 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency word
 ing + current ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or omits 
 a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 11)\n
 By the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n
 • Convert among binary\, decimal\, and hexadecimal and use binary place 
 value confidently.\n• Explain Boolean logic and the behavior/truth table
 s of NOT\, AND\, OR\, NAND\, NOR\, XOR\, and XNOR.\n• Distinguish combin
 ational from sequential logic and recognize latches/flip-flops/counters at
  a basic level.\n• Explain logic-high/logic-low levels\, noise margins\,
  pull-ups/pull-downs\, floating inputs\, and open-drain/open-collector con
 cepts.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are inten
 ded to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain 
 or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not count that it
 em as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the lin
 ked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE CO
