  use binary place value confidently.\n• Explain Boolean logic and the be
 havior/truth tables of NOT\, AND\, OR\, NAND\, NOR\, XOR\, and XNOR.\n• 
 Distinguish combinational from sequential logic and recognize latches/flip
 -flops/counters at a basic level.\n• Explain logic-high/logic-low levels
 \, noise margins\, pull-ups/pull-downs\, floating inputs\, and open-drain/
 open-collector concepts.\n• Convert binary/decimal/hex\, complete truth 
 tables\, and evaluate Boolean expressions.\n• Use logic-state reasoning 
 to predict digital outputs.\n• Recognize memory\, buses\, ports\, and ba
 sic digital-system blocks.\n• Verify digital behavior using truth tables
 \, simulation\, or measured logic signals.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned
  resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcom
 e list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items afte
 r the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a
