 .github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Component-
 level analog/digital troubleshooting and instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORI
 TY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work fi
 rst\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 12 FOCUS: LIGHT / B
 UFFER 2: Soldering + Git + CumulativeRepair\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 5.1–5.12 pl
 us cumulative weakrows\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Through-hole solder/desol
 der\, basicrework\, ESD/workmanship\, Git commits/README\; Thanksgiving-ad
 justedworkload.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- Soldering Tutorial Part 1:htt
 ps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J5Sb21qbpEQ\n- Soldering Tutorial Part2: http
 s://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fYz5nIHH0iY\n- GitHub Skills —Introduction t
 o Git:https://github.com/skills/introduction-to-github\n\nMASTERY GATE: Pr
 oduceacceptable solder joints\, repair one intentional defect\, commitphot
 os/results to Git\, and clear accumulated CETa weak rows.\n\nSYSTEMRULES: 
 Watching alone never counts. Use learn -> retrieve ->calculate/code -> bui
 ld/measure -> debug -> document. Start eachnon-exam study block with ~10 m
 inutes of spaced recall. Never use amissed session as justification for an
  unhealthy make-upmarathon.\n\nTODAY:\nStudy soldering tools\, flux\, join
 t quality\,desoldering and ESD. First 10 min: cumulative CETa recall.\n\nR
 EFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide
 \, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page number
 s in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdA
 STErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / U
 SE: Ch.20 pp.176–180 + quick ESD reread Ch.2 pp.12–13.\nQUIZ / REVIEW:
  Ch.20 quiz p.180.\nWHY: Turns soldering/ESD from a side topic into explic
 it CETa coverage plus physical bridge-job proof.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edi
 tion book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + c
 urrent ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or omits a curre
 nt topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 12)\nBy the 
 end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Exp
 lain ESD risk and use basic ESD-safe handling practices.\n• Prepare\, so
 lder\, inspect\, desolder\, and rework basic through-hole/header connectio
 ns safely.\n• Repair any previously identified weak concept before treat
 ing it as mastered.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks ab
 ove are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still ca
 nnot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not 
 count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list an
 d use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.
 \n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the lear
 ning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, wri
 te that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next
  available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
