DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfr
 ed-university/week.html?week=13\n• Search this topic: https://numberclaw2.
 github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Schematics%20%2B%20Troubleshooti
 ng\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university
 /resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Component-level analog/digital trouble
 shooting and instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Cor
 e → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repa
 ir or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 13 FOCUS: Schematics + Block/Wiring Diagrams +S
 ystematic Troubleshooting\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 6.1–6.10\; 8.xreinforcement\;
  21.4/21.7 preview\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Signaltracing\, test points\,
  pinouts\, datasheets\, expected-vs-actualmeasurements\, reproduce→measu
 re→isolate→verify.\n\nTHIS WEEK'SRESOURCES:\n- PRIMARY — SparkFun Ho
 w to Read a Schematic: https://learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/how-to-read-a-
 schematic/overview\n\nMASTERY GATE:Trace power/signal flow on an unfamilia
 r diagram\, choose next testpoints\, locate a seeded fault\, and write a c
 oncise defect/root-causenote.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts
 . Use learn ->retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> docu
 ment. Starteach non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Ne
 ver use amissed session as justification for an unhealthy make-upmarathon.
 \n\nTODAY:\nStudy only the resources tied to this week’scompetencies. Cr
 eate a one-page summary and 5–10 recall prompts. First10 min: spaced ret
 rieval from older material.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Of
 ficial Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive 
 copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. err
 ata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE 
 — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.18 pp.159–164 + selected Ch.19 pp
 .165–175 review + Appendix C pp.217–218.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.18 quiz p.
 164 + Unit 8 review p.181.\nWHY: This is the book's strongest troubleshoot
 ing/diagram/test-point block and directly supports engineering-lab work.\n
 SOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ET
 A competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book 
 differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUT
 COMES (WEEK 13)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain 
 or demonstrate:\n• Read basic schematics\, block diagrams\, wiring diagr
 ams\, pinouts\, connector tables\, and signal-flow drawings.\n• Trace po
 wer and signals from source to destination and relate schematic symbols to
  physical hardware.\n• Use datasheets to find pin functions\, ratings\, 
 timing\, operating conditions\, and reference circuits.\n• Apply a syste
 matic troubleshooting loop: verify symptom\, gather evidence\, divide/isol
 ate\, form hypothesis\, test\, repair\, verify.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe ass
 igned resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this o
 utcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items
  after the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept
  on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental reso
 urce before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigne
 d work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or 
 demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list a
 nd repair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet loggin
 g is required.
