SUMMARY:W13 • Practice — Diagram Reading & Troubleshooting Questions
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfr
 ed-university/week.html?week=13\n• Search this topic: https://numberclaw2.
 github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Schematics%20%2B%20Troubleshooti
 ng\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university
 /resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Component-level analog/digital trouble
 shooting and instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Cor
 e → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repa
 ir or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 13 FOCUS: Schematics + Block/Wiring Diagrams +S
 ystematic Troubleshooting\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 6.1–6.10\; 8.xreinforcement\;
  21.4/21.7 preview\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Signaltracing\, test points\,
  pinouts\, datasheets\, expected-vs-actualmeasurements\, reproduce→measu
 re→isolate→verify.\n\nTHIS WEEK'SRESOURCES:\n- PRIMARY — SparkFun Ho
 w to Read a Schematic: https://learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/how-to-read-a-
 schematic/overview\n\nMASTERY GATE:Trace power/signal flow on an unfamilia
 r diagram\, choose next testpoints\, locate a seeded fault\, and write a c
 oncise defect/root-causenote.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts
 . Use learn ->retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> docu
 ment. Starteach non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Ne
 ver use amissed session as justification for an unhealthy make-upmarathon.
 \n\nTODAY:\nWork fresh calculations/recognition questionswithout notes. Us
 e the official formula sheet when allowed. Target≥80%\; every miss gets 
 an ETA competency number and written correction.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP
  THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your 
 scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.
 \n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\n
 OFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.18 pp.159–16
 4 + selected Ch.19 pp.165–175 review + Appendix C pp.217–218.\nQUIZ / 
 REVIEW: Ch.18 quiz p.164 + Unit 8 review p.181.\nWHY: This is the book's s
 trongest troubleshooting/diagram/test-point block and directly supports en
 gineering-lab work.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa
  textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whe
 never the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — 
 REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 13)\nBy the end of this event\, you shoul
 d be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Use diagram/signal-path informat
 ion to choose measurement points and isolate a fault.\n• Interpret expec
 ted values from a schematic before probing.\n• Use signal tracing\, subs
 titution/known-good comparison\, continuity\, voltage\, and waveform check
 s appropriately.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above
  are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still canno
 t explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not cou
 nt that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and u
 se the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\
 nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learnin
 g outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write 
 that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next av
 ailable review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
