DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfr
 ed-university/week.html?week=16\n• Search this topic: https://numberclaw2.
 github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=STM32%20Setup%20%2B%20GPIO%20%2B
 %20SWD%20Debug\n• Lab Center: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-univers
 ity/labs.html\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred
 -university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: C + MCU bring-up + serial b
 uses + debug instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Cor
 e → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repa
 ir or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 16 FOCUS: HOLIDAY LIGHT: STM32 Setup + GPIO + S
 WDDebug\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 13.12\; 15.3/15.6\; 12.1–12.3reinforcement\nCAR
 EER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: CubeIDE\, build/flash\, Cortex-Mbasics\, GPIO\, pin 
 mux\, breakpoints\, watch variables/registers\; noChristmas-Eve session.\n
 \nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- STM32CubeIDE:https://www.st.com/content/st_com
 /en/stm32cubeide.html\n- STM32 MCUDeveloper Zone: https://www.st.com/conte
 nt/st_com/en/stm32-mcu-developer-zone.html\n\nMASTERY GATE: Build/flash a 
 GPIO project\, usebreakpoints/watch\, explain the major build/debug steps\
 , and documentone real debug issue.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never 
 counts. Uselearn -> retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -
 >document. Start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spacedrecal
 l. Never use a missed session as justification for an unhealthymake-up mar
 athon.\n\nTODAY:\nBuild button→MCU→output. Test expectedstates and one
  deliberate configuration/wiring fault. No Christmas-Evestudy block.\n\nOF
 FICIAL STM32 REFERENCES:\n• STM32CubeIDE: https://www.st.com/content/st_
 com/en/stm32cubeide.html\n• STM32CubeIDE Basics MOOC: https://www.st.com
 /content/st_com/en/support/learning/stm32-moocs/STM32CubeIDE_basics_MOOC.h
 tml\n• STM32CubeMX & CubeHAL Basics MOOC: https://www.st.com/content/st_
 com/en/support/learning/stm32-moocs/stm32cubemx-and-cubeHhal-basics.html\n
 \nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Gu
 ide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page num
 bers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6th
 EdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD 
 / USE: Targeted Ch.17 pp.149–155 review while setting up STM32.\nQUIZ / 
 REVIEW: Explain MPU/memory/I/O/control blocks without notes before the GPI
 O lab.\nWHY: The book gives architecture vocabulary\; STM32 practice turns
  it into real MCU bring-up/debug capability.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition
  book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + curre
 nt ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or omits a current t
 opic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 16)\nBy the end 
 of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Explain
  what an MCU and ARM Cortex-M core are and identify flash\, RAM\, GPIO\, c
 locks\, and peripherals in an STM32 system.\n• Create/configure a basic 
 STM32 project in STM32CubeIDE/CubeMX.\n• Configure GPIO input/output and
  understand pin multiplexing at a working level.\n• Build\, flash\, run\
 , and reset firmware on a real board.\n• Use SWD debugging: breakpoints\
 , single-step\, watch variables\, and basic register inspection.\n• Sepa
 rate a firmware problem from a board/power/configuration problem during br
 ing-up.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are inte
 nded to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain
  or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not count that i
 tem as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the li
 nked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nWEEK-END
  MASTERY RULE\nThis practical is the cumulative proof point for the week. 
 The week is Green only when the knowledge can be used on real hardware/cod
 e/measurements without following a step-by-step tutorial.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLE
 TION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes bel
 ow. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one conce
 pt on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next available review
  block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
END:VALARM
