DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfr
 ed-university/week.html?week=18\n• Search this topic: https://numberclaw2.
 github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=I2C/SPI%20%2B%20Logic%20Analyzer
 %20%2B%20Sensors/Actuators\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.git
 hub.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: C + MCU bring-
 up + serial buses + debug instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core 
 → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep
  Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nNeed by Week 18. Confirm logic analyze
 r and leads\, one supported I2C or SPI sensor/peripheral breakout\, jumper
  wires\, pull-ups if required\, datasheet\, and safe voltage compatibility
  with the MCU.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associ
 ate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the 
 PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://
 www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING 
 OUTCOMES\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demo
 nstrate:\n• Know what equipment/parts are required for the next practica
 l session and what each item is for.\n• Confirm every critical item is r
 eady\, compatible\, and safe to use before the lab begins.\n• Identify a
 ny missing item early enough to obtain or substitute it without cancelling
  the hands-on work.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks ab
 ove are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still ca
 nnot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not 
 count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list an
 d use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.
 \n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the lear
 ning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, wri
 te that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next
  available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Equipment\,Embedded\,CETa
