SUMMARY:W17 • Learn — UART Communication & Implementation
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfr
 ed-university/week.html?week=17\n• Search this topic: https://numberclaw2.
 github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=UART%20%2B%20Python%20Serial\n
 • Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/res
 ources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: C + MCU bring-up + serial buses + debug in
 strumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive
 . Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra dep
 th.\n\nWEEK 17 FOCUS: HOLIDAY LIGHT: UART + Python Serial + ComputerApplic
 ations\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 16.1–16.10\; 12.1–12.4\nCAREER/EMBEDDEDPURPOSE
 : UART framing/baud\, terminal use\, Python pySerial logging\,basic softwa
 re/storage/backups/networking\; no New-Year’s-Evesession.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S
  RESOURCES:\n- Serial Communication — SparkFun:https://learn.sparkfun.co
 m/tutorials/serial-communication/all\n-pySerial docs: https://pyserial.rea
 dthedocs.io/\n\nMASTERY GATE:Send/receive MCU serial data\, parse/log it i
 n Python\, explain basiccomputer/software/networking concepts\, and recove
 r from a malformedresponse.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. 
 Use learn ->retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> docume
 nt. Starteach non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Neve
 r use amissed session as justification for an unhealthy make-upmarathon.\n
 \nTODAY:\nLearn TX/RX/GND\, framing/baud\, terminal use.Implement MCU stat
 us output.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate 
 CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRIN
 TED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.
 etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIG
 NMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.16 pp.144–146 ports/interfaces + selected Ch.17 pp
 .149–155.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Short current-competency recall set\; book is 
 background\, not the whole UART/Python skill.\nWHY: The 2016 book covers c
 omputer/port concepts but external UART and Python material is required fo
 r current practical depth.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the prima
 ry CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata cont
 rol whenever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TOD
 AY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 17)\nBy the end of this event\, yo
 u should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Explain UART TX\, RX\, gr
 ound/reference\, baud rate\, frame format\, and asynchronous serial commun
 ication.\n• Send and receive UART data between an STM32 and a host compu
 ter.\n• Use a terminal/serial monitor to inspect traffic and diagnose ba
 sic framing/configuration problems.\n• Use Python/pySerial to open a por
 t\, configure timeout/baud\, send commands\, read responses\, and close cl
 eanly.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are inten
 ded to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain 
 or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not count that it
 em as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the lin
 ked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE CO
 MPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes
  below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one c
 oncept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next available re
 view block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
