 n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nO
 FFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.16 pp.144–146
  ports/interfaces + selected Ch.17 pp.149–155.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Short cur
 rent-competency recall set\; book is background\, not the whole UART/Pytho
 n skill.\nWHY: The 2016 book covers computer/port concepts but external UA
 RT and Python material is required for current practical depth.\nSOURCE RU
 LE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA compete
 ncy wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book differs o
 r omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WE
 EK 17)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demons
 trate:\n• Explain UART TX\, RX\, ground/reference\, baud rate\, frame fo
 rmat\, and asynchronous serial communication.\n• Send and receive UART d
 ata between an STM32 and a host computer.\n• Use a terminal/serial monit
 or to inspect traffic and diagnose basic framing/configuration problems.\n
 • Use Python/pySerial to open a port\, configure timeout/baud\, send com
 mands\, read responses\, and close cleanly.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigne
 d resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outco
 me list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items aft
 er the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on 
 a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resource
  before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned wo
 rk\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demo
 nstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and r
 epair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is
  required.
