SUMMARY:W18 • Learn — I²C\, SPI\, Logic Analyzer & Sensors
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfr
 ed-university/week.html?week=18\n• Search this topic: https://numberclaw2.
 github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=I2C/SPI%20%2B%20Logic%20Analyzer
 %20%2B%20Sensors/Actuators\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.git
 hub.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: C + MCU bring-
 up + serial buses + debug instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core 
 → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep
  Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 18 FOCUS: I2C/SPI + Logic Analyze
 r +Sensors/Actuators\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 12.5\; 13.5/13.7–13.12\; 8.10–8.
 12reinforcement\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: One real I2C or SPI peripheral\,
 bus capture\, pull-ups/chip-select/clocking\, sensor units\, PWM/outputcon
 trol.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- I2C Tutorial — SparkFun:https://learn
 .sparkfun.com/tutorials/i2c/all\n- SPI Tutorial — SparkFun:https://learn
 .sparkfun.com/tutorials/serial-peripheral-interface-spi/all\n- Saleae supp
 ort: https://support.saleae.com/\n\nMASTERY GATE:Implement one board-level
  bus\, capture and interpret transactions\,diagnose one bus fault\, and dr
 ive/read a real peripheral.\n\nSYSTEMRULES: Watching alone never counts. U
 se learn -> retrieve ->calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> documen
 t. Start eachnon-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never
  use amissed session as justification for an unhealthy make-upmarathon.\n\
 nTODAY:\nStudy only the resources tied to this week’scompetencies. Creat
 e a one-page summary and 5–10 recall prompts. First10 min: spaced retrie
 val from older material.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Offic
 ial Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive cop
 y and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata
 : https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE —
  V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Use Ch.16/17 as reference only\; current 
 ETA competency wording + I2C/SPI tutorials control the interface lesson.\n
 QUIZ / REVIEW: Unit 7 review pp.157–158 as cumulative digital review.\nW
 HY: I2C/SPI/modern interface expectations are not fully covered by this ol
 der book\, so current ETA + hands-on resources fill the gap.\nSOURCE RULE:
  The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency
  wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or o
 mits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 
 18)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstra
 te:\n• Explain I2C controller/target roles\, SDA/SCL\, addressing\, pull
 -ups\, start/stop\, read/write\, ACK/NACK\, and basic transactions.\n• E
 xplain SPI controller/peripheral roles\, SCLK\, MOSI\, MISO\, chip select\
 , transaction framing\, and the idea of clock mode.\n• Choose I2C or SPI
  appropriately for a simple peripheral and wire it correctly.\n• Use a l
 ogic analyzer to capture and decode UART and the chosen I2C/SPI bus.\n\nCO
 VERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover
  every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstra
 te one of these items after the session\, do not count that item as comple
 te. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked official
  or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RUL
 E\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If y
 ou cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a 
 short catch-up list and repair it during the next available review block. 
 No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
