DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfr
 ed-university/week.html?week=18\n• Search this topic: https://numberclaw2.
 github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=I2C/SPI%20%2B%20Logic%20Analyzer
 %20%2B%20Sensors/Actuators\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.git
 hub.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: C + MCU bring-
 up + serial buses + debug instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core 
 → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep
  Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 18 FOCUS: I2C/SPI + Logic Analyze
 r +Sensors/Actuators\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 12.5\; 13.5/13.7–13.12\; 8.10–8.
 12reinforcement\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: One real I2C or SPI peripheral\,
 bus capture\, pull-ups/chip-select/clocking\, sensor units\, PWM/outputcon
 trol.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- I2C Tutorial — SparkFun:https://learn
 .sparkfun.com/tutorials/i2c/all\n- SPI Tutorial — SparkFun:https://learn
 .sparkfun.com/tutorials/serial-peripheral-interface-spi/all\n- Saleae supp
 ort: https://support.saleae.com/\n\nMASTERY GATE:Implement one board-level
  bus\, capture and interpret transactions\,diagnose one bus fault\, and dr
 ive/read a real peripheral.\n\nSYSTEMRULES: Watching alone never counts. U
 se learn -> retrieve ->calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> documen
 t. Start eachnon-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never
  use amissed session as justification for an unhealthy make-upmarathon.\n\
 nTODAY:\nWork fresh calculations/recognition questionswithout notes. Use t
 he official formula sheet when allowed. Target≥80%\; every miss gets an 
 ETA competency number and written correction.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP TH
 ESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your sca
 nned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n
 • ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOF
 FICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Use Ch.16/17 as ref
 erence only\; current ETA competency wording + I2C/SPI tutorials control t
 he interface lesson.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Unit 7 review pp.157–158 as cumulat
 ive digital review.\nWHY: I2C/SPI/modern interface expectations are not fu
 lly covered by this older book\, so current ETA + hands-on resources fill 
 the gap.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. 
 Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the o
 lder book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LE
 ARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 18)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able t
 o explain or demonstrate:\n• Explain I2C controller/target roles\, SDA/S
 CL\, addressing\, pull-ups\, start/stop\, read/write\, ACK/NACK\, and basi
 c transactions.\n• Explain SPI controller/peripheral roles\, SCLK\, MOSI
 \, MISO\, chip select\, transaction framing\, and the idea of clock mode.\
 n• Choose I2C or SPI appropriately for a simple peripheral and wire it c
 orrectly.\n• Use a logic analyzer to capture and decode UART and the cho
 sen I2C/SPI bus.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above
  are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still canno
 t explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not cou
 nt that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and u
 se the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\
 nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learnin
 g outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write 
 that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next av
 ailable review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
