 ps://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/progress.html\n• Search Every
 thing: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html\n• Engi
 neering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.h
 tml\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete 
 the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nBefo
 re Spring coursework becomes heavy\, enter your actual GSU Perimeter class
 /lab times\, commute\, known exam windows\, and weekly homework load. Comp
 are them to January-April study blocks. School wins conflicts. If the real
  class schedule materially changes availability\, revise the V5 calendar i
 nstead of trying to make up missed study with marathons.\n\nREFERENCE HUB 
 — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: u
 se your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASS
 IGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet
 .pdf\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES\nBy the end of this eve
 nt\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Know the reduced s
 tudy cadence once college classes begin.\n• Understand that school exam 
 weeks take priority and missed self-study is rescheduled rather than cramm
 ed.\n• Know which course milestones must remain protected even when the 
 weekly schedule flexes.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and task
 s above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you stil
 l cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do 
 not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up lis
 t and use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the 
 gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the 
