DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Project Center: https://numberclaw2.github.io/a
 lfred-university/projects.html\n• Progress Portal: https://numberclaw2.git
 hub.io/alfred-university/progress.html\n• Search Everything: https://nbe
 rclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html\n• Engineering Library: h
 ttps://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nRESOURCE PRIO
 RITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work 
 first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nProject 1 design begin
 s next week. Draft the BOM\, identify parts already owned\, order only ite
 ms justified by the requirements\, confirm delivery dates\, and record sub
 stitutions/risks. No feature-creep purchases.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP TH
 ESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your sca
 nned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n
 • ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nAF
 TER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES\nBy the end of this event\, you s
 hould be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Know what equipment/parts ar
 e required for the next practical session and what each item is for.\n• 
 Confirm every critical item is ready\, compatible\, and safe to use before
  the lab begins.\n• Identify any missing item early enough to obtain or 
 substitute it without cancelling the hands-on work.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe
  assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in th
 is outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these i
 tems after the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the con
 cept on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental 
 resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the ass
 igned work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain
  or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up li
 st and repair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet lo
 gging is required.
