 ssessment Center: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/assessment
 s.html\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-univer
 sity/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Broad CETa general-electronics cov
 erage plus mixed-domain troubleshooting.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core →
  Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Di
 ve for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 21 FOCUS: CETa Final Review I: Formu
 la + Component +Diagram + Safety Gates\nETA/CETa SCOPE: All 1.0–21.0\; o
 fficial errataapplied\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Consolidate without pausin
 g embeddedmomentum\; begin Project 1 requirements/block diagram during non
 -examwork.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- ETA CETa competencies:https://www.
 etai.org/comps/CETa_comps.pdf\n- ETA Common Formulas:https://www.etai.org/
 Common_Formulas.pdf\n- ETA 6th Ed. Errata:https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErr
 ataSheet.pdf\n- ETA electronics page:https://www.etai.org/electronics.html
 \n\nMASTERY GATE: Formula drill≥90%\; component/diagram/safety gates gre
 en\; Saturday: official ASTPractice Exam #1 under 2-hour limit\; map every
  miss to an ETAcompetency row.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never count
 s. Use learn-> retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> doc
 ument.Start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. N
 everuse a missed session as justification for an unhealthy make-upmarathon
 .\n\nTODAY:\nFirst 10 min cumulative recall. Work fresh formulasfrom the o
 fficial sheet to ≥90%. Identify unfamiliar componentsymbols/packages/rat
 ings. Apply current ETA errata.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n
 • Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google 
 Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-e
 d. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY 
 GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Review formula p.224\, symbol/re
 ference p.222\, Appendix C pp.217–218\, weak chapter quizzes and current
  ETA errata.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Saturday: Book Practice Exam #1\, pp.194–20
 1\, under a 2-hour limit. Map every miss to the current ETA competency num
 ber.\nWHY: The book practice exam checks broad recall\, while current ETA 
 competency rows prevent outdated book coverage from defining readiness.\nS
 OURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA
  competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book d
 iffers or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTC
 OMES (WEEK 21)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain o
 r demonstrate:\n• Recall and apply the core formula families required by
  the current CETa scope.\n• Identify common components\, symbols\, diagr
 ams\, instruments\, and safety practices quickly and accurately.\n• Choo
 se the correct measurement/test method from a scenario.\n• Navigate mixe
 d electronics questions without relying on one-topic-at-a-time cues.\n• 
 Identify weak competency numbers and repair specific gaps instead of rerea
 ding everything.\n• Demonstrate readiness for full-length CETa practice 
 work.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intend
 ed to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain o
 r demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not count that ite
 m as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the link
 ed official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COM
 PLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes 
 below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one co
 ncept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next available rev
 iew block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
