 Project%20Setup\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfr
 ed-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Broad CETa general-electr
 onics coverage plus mixed-domain troubleshooting.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa
  Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; us
 e Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 23 FOCUS: CETa Exam Target 
 + Project 1 Setup\nETA/CETaSCOPE: Final weak rows only\; no new CETa conte
 nt\nCAREER/EMBEDDEDPURPOSE: Light review\, register/book exam if two 85% s
 cores achieved\;initialize repo and bench setup.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:
 \n- ETAelectronics / exam info: https://www.etai.org/electronics.html\n- E
 TACETa competencies: https://www.etai.org/comps/CETa_comps.pdf\n\nMASTERYG
 ATE: If two practice scores are ≥85%\, sit CETa when booked. If not\,pos
 tpone the exam without changing the embedded plan and continuetargeted wea
 k-area repair.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts.Use learn -> r
 etrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug ->document. Start each
  non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spacedrecall. Never use a missed
  session as justification for an unhealthymake-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nIf 
 both full practice scores are ≥85%\,finalize exam logistics. Otherwise w
 ork only the remaining weakcompetency rows. Keep review light.\n\nREFERENC
 E HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th 
 ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BO
 OK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrat
 aSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: No 
 new book reading. Use weak book chapters\, p.223 answers\, p.224 formulas 
 and current ETA errata only for targeted repairs.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Saturday
 : current official AST Practice run #2 under a 2-hour limit. CETa-ready on
 ly after ≥85% twice.\nWHY: Prevents endless rereading: final readiness i
 s driven by current official practice performance and exact weak competenc
 y repair.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook.
  Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the 
 older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED L
 EARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 23)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able 
 to explain or demonstrate:\n• Complete the CETa readiness gate using cur
 rent practice performance and targeted repairs.\n• Organize the Project 
 1 repository\, folders\, README skeleton\, issue list\, and evidence locat
 ions.\n• Prepare the bench\, board\, cables\, instruments\, firmware too
 lchain\, and parts for controlled bring-up.\n• Confirm Project 1 require
 ments\, interfaces\, test cases\, and safety limits before powering hardwa
 re.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intended
  to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or 
 demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not count that item 
 as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked
  official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPL
 ETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes be
 low. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one conc
 ept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next available revie
 w block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
