 ps://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/progress.html\n• Search Every
 thing: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html\n• Engi
 neering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.h
 tml\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete 
 the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nSit 
 the real CETa only if two full official practice runs areat least 85%. ETA
 ’s actual passing score is 75%\, but this plan keepsthe stronger interna
 l gate. If not ready\, move the real exam\; do notpause Project 1.\n\nREFE
 RENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 
 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers i
 n BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTE
 rrataSheet.pdf\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES\nBy the end o
 f this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• No new t
 echnical content is assigned in this event.\n• Use this checkpoint to ve
 rify that the preceding mastery gate is actually demonstrable.\n• Do not
  mark the milestone complete because the date arrived\; the evidence must 
 be complete.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are
  intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot ex
 plain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not count t
 hat item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use t
 he linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIM
 PLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning ou
 tcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that
  one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next availa
 ble review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
