 github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=CETa%20Readiness%20Gate%20%2B%20
 Project%20Setup\n• Assessment Center: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred
 -university/assessments.html\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.g
 ithub.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Broad CETa g
 eneral-electronics coverage plus mixed-domain troubleshooting.\nRESOURCE P
 RIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required wo
 rk first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 23 FOCUS: CETa
  Exam Target + Project 1 Setup\nETA/CETaSCOPE: Final weak rows only\; no n
 ew CETa content\nCAREER/EMBEDDEDPURPOSE: Light review\, register/book exam
  if two 85% scores achieved\;initialize repo and bench setup.\n\nTHIS WEEK
 'S RESOURCES:\n- ETAelectronics / exam info: https://www.etai.org/electron
 ics.html\n- ETACETa competencies: https://www.etai.org/comps/CETa_comps.pd
 f\n\nMASTERYGATE: If two practice scores are ≥85%\, sit CETa when booked
 . If not\,postpone the exam without changing the embedded plan and continu
 etargeted weak-area repair.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts.U
 se learn -> retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug ->documen
 t. Start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spacedrecall. Never
  use a missed session as justification for an unhealthymake-up marathon.\n
 \nTODAY:\nIf your actual CETa exam is booked fortoday\, use this block for
  the exam. If not\, use it for targetedweak-area review and Project 1 setu
 p\; do not invent an exam appointment.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LIN
 KS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Go
 ogle Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 
 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL S
 TUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: No new book reading. Use we
 ak book chapters\, p.223 answers\, p.224 formulas and current ETA errata o
 nly for targeted repairs.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Saturday: current official AST P
 ractice run #2 under a 2-hour limit. CETa-ready only after ≥85% twice.\n
 WHY: Prevents endless rereading: final readiness is driven by current offi
 cial practice performance and exact weak competency repair.\nSOURCE RULE: 
 The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency 
 wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or om
 its a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 2
 3)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrat
 e:\n• Complete the CETa readiness gate using current practice performanc
 e and targeted repairs.\n• Organize the Project 1 repository\, folders\,
  README skeleton\, issue list\, and evidence locations.\n• Prepare the b
 ench\, board\, cables\, instruments\, firmware toolchain\, and parts for c
 ontrolled bring-up.\n• Confirm Project 1 requirements\, interfaces\, tes
 t cases\, and safety limits before powering hardware.\n• Distinguish 're
 ady to build' from 'still collecting resources.'\n• Begin Project 1 with
  a reproducible\, documented setup.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resour
 ces and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list.
  If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the s
 ession\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short 
 catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resource before 
 closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, the
 n check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate 
 an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it
  during the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is require
 d.
