SUMMARY:W24 • Project 1 Learn — Safe Hardware Bring-Up
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfr
 ed-university/week.html?week=24\n• Search this topic: https://numberclaw2.
 github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Project%201%20Hardware%20Bring-U
 p\n• Lab Center: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/labs.html
 \n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/r
 esources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Portfolio-grade hardware/firmware/test e
 vidence.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Comp
 lete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\
 nWEEK 24 FOCUS: Project 1 Hardware Bring-Up\nETA/CETa SCOPE:Maintenance re
 trieval only\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Power\, GPIO\,button\, controlled o
 utput\, UART\, clean wiring\, railmeasurements/current draw.\n\nTHIS WEEK'
 S RESOURCES:\n- STM32 MCUDeveloper Zone: https://www.st.com/content/st_com
 /en/stm32-mcu-developer-zone.html\n- ETA Common Formulas:https://www.etai.
 org/Common_Formulas.pdf\n\nMASTERY GATE: Boardpowers safely\, core I/O and
  UART work\, measurements are documented\,and at least one bring-up failur
 e has a root-cause story.\n\nSYSTEMRULES: Watching alone never counts. Use
  learn -> retrieve ->calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> document.
  Start eachnon-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never u
 se amissed session as justification for an unhealthy make-upmarathon.\n\nT
 ODAY:\nFirst 10 min: spaced recall from prior weeks. Studythis week’s sc
 oped material and make a one-page memory summary. Complete8–12 fresh CET
 a questions when ETA content applies. School work takespriority during exa
 m-heavy weeks.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associ
 ate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the 
 PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://
 www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK A
 SSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Reference Ch.11 pp.85–90\, Ch.18 pp.159–164 and
  Ch.19 pp.165–175 during hardware bring-up.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: No new book 
 quiz\; cite the relevant page in your troubleshooting notes when it inform
 s a decision.\nWHY: Reuses CETa material as real engineering-lab procedure
  instead of separating certification knowledge from job skill.\nSOURCE RUL
 E: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competen
 cy wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or
  omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEE
 K 24)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonst
 rate:\n• Perform safe first power-up using visual inspection\, continuit
 y checks\, a current-limited supply\, and measured power rails.\n• Verif
 y board power\, ground\, reset/boot conditions\, GPIO\, and UART before ad
 ding complexity.\n• Measure voltage/current and record baseline current 
 draw.\n• Use SWD/UART diagnostics to separate hardware\, firmware\, and 
 configuration faults.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks 
 above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still 
 cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do no
 t count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list 
 and use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the ga
 p.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the le
 arning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, w
 rite that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the ne
 xt available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
