SUMMARY:W25 • Project 1 Learn — Sensor & Interface Integration
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfr
 ed-university/week.html?week=25\n• Search this topic: https://numberclaw2.
 github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Project%201%20Sensor%20/%20Inter
 face%20Integration\n• Lab Center: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-uni
 versity/labs.html\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/al
 fred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Portfolio-grade hardwar
 e/firmware/test evidence.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core 
 → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair
  or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 25 FOCUS: Project 1 Sensor / InterfaceIntegration
 \nETA/CETa SCOPE: 12.5/13.x/8.x spacedreview\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Int
 egrate I2C/SPI sensor\, convert rawdata to engineering units\, capture bus
  traffic and handledisconnect/address faults.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n-
  I2C Tutorial —SparkFun: https://learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/i2c/all\n-
  SPI Tutorial —SparkFun: https://learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/serial-per
 ipheral-interface-spi/all\n- Saleae support: https://support.saleae.com/\n
 \nMASTERYGATE: Sensor/interface works end-to-end\, analyzer capture isinte
 rpretable\, and one physical or protocol fault is diagnosed anddocumented.
 \n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn ->retrieve -> cal
 culate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> document. Starteach non-exam stud
 y block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use amissed session as ju
 stification for an unhealthy make-upmarathon.\n\nTODAY:\nFirst 10 min: spa
 ced recall from prior weeks. Studythis week’s scoped material and make a
  one-page memory summary. Complete8–12 fresh CETa questions when ETA con
 tent applies. School work takespriority during exam-heavy weeks.\n\nREFERE
 NCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6t
 h ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in 
 BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErr
 ataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: R
 eference Ch.16 pp.144–147 and Ch.17 pp.149–155\; use current ETA + dat
 asheets/tutorials for the actual I2C/SPI device.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: No new bo
 ok quiz.\nWHY: Book architecture supports the concept\, while the project 
 proves modern interface implementation.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book
  is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ET
 A errata control whenever the older book differs or omits a current topic.
 \n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 25)\nBy the end of th
 is event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Integrate th
 e chosen I2C/SPI sensor or peripheral into Project 1.\n• Read raw regist
 ers/data and convert values into meaningful engineering units.\n• Verify
  bus activity with a logic analyzer and correlate decoded traffic with fir
 mware behavior.\n• Handle missing device\, wrong address/configuration\,
  timeout\, or invalid-data conditions.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned res
 ources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome li
 st. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after th
 e session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a sho
 rt catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resource befo
 re closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, 
 then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstra
 te an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair
  it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is requ
 ired.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
