SUMMARY:W26 • Project 1 Learn — Firmware Architecture
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfr
 ed-university/week.html?week=26\n• Search this topic: https://numberclaw2.
 github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Project%201%20Firmware%20Archite
 cture\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-univers
 ity/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Portfolio-grade hardware/firmware/t
 est evidence.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive.
  Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra dept
 h.\n\nWEEK 26 FOCUS: Project 1 Firmware Architecture\nETA/CETaSCOPE: 13.10
 –13.12 spaced review\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Timers\,interrupts\, PWM\
 , nonblocking FSM\, timeouts\, error codes anddiagnostic output.\n\nTHIS W
 EEK'S RESOURCES:\n- STM32 MCU DeveloperZone: https://www.st.com/content/st
 _com/en/stm32-mcu-developer-zone.html\n\nMASTERY GATE: Firmware runs witho
 ut long blocking delays\, timing ismeasured\, error paths are exercised\, 
 and architecture can be explainedat interview depth.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watc
 hing alone never counts. Uselearn -> retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/m
 easure -> debug ->document. Start each non-exam study block with ~10 minut
 es of spacedrecall. Never use a missed session as justification for an unh
 ealthymake-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nFirst 10 min: spaced recall from priorw
 eeks. Study this week’s scoped material and make a one-page memorysummar
 y. Complete 8–12 fresh CETa questions when ETA content applies.School wo
 rk takes priority during exam-heavy weeks.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE
  LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanne
 d/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• 
 ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICI
 AL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Reference Ch.17 pp.151
 –155 and Ch.16 logic/sequential sections pp.136–143.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: E
 xplain your firmware state machine and hardware-control flow without the b
 ook open.\nWHY: Connects book control/programming concepts to structured e
 mbedded firmware.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa t
 extbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whene
 ver the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — RE
 QUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 26)\nBy the end of this event\, you should 
 be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Organize Project 1 firmware into u
 nderstandable modules with clear responsibilities.\n• Use a nonblocking 
 finite-state machine for system behavior.\n• Use timers/interrupts where
  appropriate without creating timing-dependent chaos.\n• Implement timeo
 uts\, error states\, diagnostic messages\, and recoverable fault handling.
 \n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intended to
  cover every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or dem
 onstrate one of these items after the session\, do not count that item as 
 complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked of
 ficial or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETI
 ON RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes below
 . If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept
  on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next available review b
 lock. No spreadsheet logging is required.
