DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfr
 ed-university/week.html?week=28\n• Search this topic: https://numberclaw2.
 github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Fault%20Injection%20%2B%20Troubl
 eshooting%20%2B%20Test%20Report\n• Engineering Library: https://nberclaw
 2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Portfolio
 -grade hardware/firmware/test evidence.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → 
 Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Div
 e for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 28 FOCUS: Fault Injection + Troublesh
 ooting + TestReport\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 6.x/8.x/21.4/21.7 spaced review\nCARE
 ER/EMBEDDEDPURPOSE: Seed sensor disconnect\, wrong address\, bad wire\, ti
 meout\,config error\, power fault and firmware defect\; useone-change-at-a
 -time diagnosis.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- ETA CETacompetencies: https:
 //www.etai.org/comps/CETa_comps.pdf\n\nMASTERY GATE:At least three intervi
 ew-ready failure stories\, including onephysical/electrical fault\, each w
 ithreproduce→measure→isolate→fix→verify evidence.\n\nSYSTEM RULES:
  Watchingalone never counts. Use learn -> retrieve -> calculate/code ->bui
 ld/measure -> debug -> document. Start each non-exam study block with~10 m
 inutes of spaced recall. Never use a missed session asjustification for an
  unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nFirst 10min: spaced recall from pr
 ior weeks. Study this week’s scoped materialand make a one-page memory s
 ummary. Complete 8–12 fresh CETa questionswhen ETA content applies. Scho
 ol work takes priority during exam-heavyweeks.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP T
 HESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your sc
 anned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n
 • ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOF
 FICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Reference Ch.18 pp.
 159–164 + Ch.22 pp.188–193 + Appendix C pp.217–218.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: 
 Use troubleshooting/technical-writing questions as retrieval\; focus on ev
 idence quality.\nWHY: Fault injection and test reports are where CETa trou
 bleshooting turns into employer-ready proof.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition
  book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + curre
 nt ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or omits a current t
 opic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 28)\nBy the end 
 of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Design 
 and execute deliberate fault-injection tests.\n• Use the troubleshooting
  sequence: reproduce\, measure\, isolate\, hypothesize\, test\, fix\, and 
 verify.\n• Distinguish hardware\, firmware\, interface\, test-fixture\, 
 power\, and host-script faults.\n• Collect DMM/scope/logic-analyzer/log 
 evidence that supports root cause.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resourc
 es and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. 
 If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the se
 ssion\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short c
 atch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resource before c
 losing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then
  check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate a
 n outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it 
 during the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required
 .
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
